35,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, it turns out some of us have much less room to give than others. It would be quite unfair to just keep things as they are.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've seen that ""better"" solutions can actually make things worse. A bin house might look cleaner, but the smell in August is unbearable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Guys, the costs are way higher than I thought! A shelter is super expensive, but the ward helps pay for some of it!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've learned that most complaints come from just one person, and even the ""perfect"" bin house at the station block led to more arguments.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I have seen that the clock is a demanding master. The time spent managing this is more than we realize, and it falls on too few shoulders.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, if the complaints are from one person, we can't let that person dictate a plan that keeps the burden on one house.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, you're right about the time. But if we implement a strict supervision rotation, we might just be trading a smell for a schedule we all hate.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"But if we use the subsidy, we can get a shelter without everyone paying a huge amount! We just need to split it right!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand, but I'm worried that if we push too hard for ""fairness"" in measurements, we might damage our friendships further.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Harmony is not the absence of conflict, but the ability to handle it. We must find a way to share the time, not just the cost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, friendship is great, but not when it's based on one person doing all the work. I'm not signing anything that ignores the frontage reality.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Let's be logical. A shelter smells, and supervision takes too much time. We need a middle ground that doesn't create a new daily annoyance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I can help with the math! If we use the subsidy, we can make it cheap for everyone. Let's just get a shelter and be done with it!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Mizuki, maybe a simpler arrangement with a clear, gentle rotation would be better than a big installation that we'll fight over later.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,Let us remember that the smallest act of kindness is worth more than the grandest intention. A shared schedule is a shared kindness.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,I'm ready to see the options. I just hope they actually address the space issue.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I'll vote for whatever minimizes the long-term daily stress for everyone, not just the immediate cost.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'll vote for the one that's cheapest for the people who don't have much money!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'll vote for the option that feels most sustainable for our relationships. I want us to be able to talk again.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,I shall vote for the path that ensures no single person is worn down by the weight of the routine.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
